WEBVTT

00:00:02.778 --> 00:00:11.702
Lesson 16 found: at 5000 rpm the crank-pin force peaks at about 752 N. Now WenQuest FEA checks whether the needle-bar crank can take it

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:20.701
The part is the needle-bar crank; ForceDirection and SpinAxis are helper lines: pin centre to shaft centre, and the upper-shaft axis

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:32.284
Switch to the FEM workbench and create an Analysis

00:00:32.284 --> 00:00:44.284
Constraint 1: fix the shaft bore. Fixed boundary condition, Add, click the bore surface, OK

00:00:45.802 --> 00:00:57.802
Load 1: the crank-pin force. Force load, add the pin-hole face, 752.5 N; direction: select the ForceDirection line, click Direction

00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:23.502
Load 2: centrifugal. Centrifugal load, mode Solid, add the crank; axis: the SpinAxis line; 83.333 Hz (5000 rpm)

00:01:37.152 --> 00:01:47.702
No need to set up mesh or solver. Click Compute and check: for a hand-built analysis, pick the material first — library values have sources, listed in the report

00:01:47.702 --> 00:01:54.201
Pick 45-QT: steel 45, quenched and tempered, yield strength 355 MPa

00:01:54.201 --> 00:02:03.376
It meshes by itself, refines level by level to see if results converge, and checks that reactions balance the loads. Takes a minute or two

00:02:03.376 --> 00:02:10.702
If a check fails, no safety factor is given — better to say “unknown” than report a number that may be wrong

00:02:10.702 --> 00:02:14.200
(About 1 min on this computer — skipped in the video)

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:22.625
Done: overall trust verdict “pass”

00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:27.626
Stress (von Mises): max about 8.4 MPa

00:02:27.626 --> 00:02:34.725
Safety factor = yield 355 ÷ 8.4 ≈ 42: plenty of margin. To lighten it or switch to aluminium, compute again

00:02:34.725 --> 00:02:46.725
All four checks pass: reaction balance, mesh quality, convergence of max stress and displacement (levels within 0.2%). Details go into the report: next part
